```cs
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX >= 0, "The index of x after insertion is more than or equal to 0");
```

Please adapt and adjust as per your requirements. If the index value might be -1, then the second argument to the Assert method can be more detailed, for easier understanding of what's the problem.--------------------This is the C# code that uses "Debug.Assert" with the appropriate messages:

```cs
using System.Diagnostics;

public void PUT_InsertContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x, int index)
{
    int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;

    Debug.Assert(index <= Old_arrListCount && index >= 0, "Index is out of range");

    int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
    bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    arrList.Insert(index, x);

    int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int New_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x); 
    int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x); 
    bool New_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX >= 0, "New_arrListIndexOfX is less than 0");
    Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount > Old_arrListCount, "New_arrListCount is not greater than Old_arrListCount after insertion");
    Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX >= Old_arrListIndexOfX, "New_arrListIndexOfX is less than Old_arrListIndexOfX");
    Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX >= Old_arrListLastIndexOfX, "New_arrListIndexOfX is less than Old_arrListIndexOfX");
    Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == Old_arrListContainsX, "New_arrListContainsX is not equal to Old_arrListContainsX");
}
```

These Debug.Assert statements will validate that the values of index, count of the list after and before insertion, index of x before and after insertion, last index of x before and after insertion, and whether X is contained in the list after and before insertion remain the same or modified as expected. If not, an error will be thrown and a debugger will stop at the point of the error.--------------------The output assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ index of x after insertion is more than or equal to 0" would be:

```csharp
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX >= 0, "index of x after insertion is less than 0");
```
This assertion checks if the index of x (`New_arrListIndexOfX`) after the insertion is greater or equal to 0. If it's lesser than 0, this statement triggers a debug assertion.--------------------